275 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H5
/T (The current digital library management system used for publishing and content distribution involves centralized, manual, and third-party-controlled processes that are prone to data manipulation, piracy, and lack of transparency. This conventional method is inefficient and often results in unauthorized sharing, unfair royalty distribution, and inaccurate record keeping. To address these issues, this paper proposes the use of blockchain technology to develop a decentralized digital library platform called SmartShelf, which ensures data integrity, transparency, and security. The blockchain-based SmartShelf model provides an immutable and decentralized public ledger that enhances the accuracy and traceability of digital content ownership. By eliminating intermediaries, SmartShelf can automate royalty distribution, streamline transactions in real time, and reduce the operational costs and risks associated with digital content management.)
/E (The current digital library management system used for publishing and content distribution involves centralized, manual, and third-party-controlled processes that are prone to data manipulation, piracy, and lack of transparency. This conventional method is inefficient and often results in unauthorized sharing, unfair royalty distribution, and inaccurate record keeping. To address these issues, this paper proposes the use of blockchain technology to develop a decentralized digital library platform called SmartShelf, which ensures data integrity, transparency, and security. The blockchain-based SmartShelf model provides an immutable and decentralized public ledger that enhances the accuracy and traceability of digital content ownership. By eliminating intermediaries, SmartShelf can automate royalty distribution, streamline transactions in real time, and reduce the operational costs and risks associated with digital content management.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
