280 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/T (The primary objective of this paper is to explore how blockchain technology can revolutionize digital publishing by ensuring secure ownership records, enabling transparent revenue tracking, and preventing piracy through cryptographic algorithms and smart contracts. This paper will first discuss the limitations of traditional digital library systems, including security, efficiency, and transparency, and then examine how blockchain-based SmartShelf addresses these challenges through decentralized and automated content management.)
/E (The primary objective of this paper is to explore how blockchain technology can revolutionize digital publishing by ensuring secure ownership records, enabling transparent revenue tracking, and preventing piracy through cryptographic algorithms and smart contracts. This paper will first discuss the limitations of traditional digital library systems, including security, efficiency, and transparency, and then examine how blockchain-based SmartShelf addresses these challenges through decentralized and automated content management.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
